Accurate diagnostics are indispensable for effective management of diseases, leading to better patient care and clinical outcomes, increase affordability by reducing overall therapy cost and also reduce antimicrobial resistance.
The Sustainable Development Goal (SDG) 3.8 sets the following target for 2030: achieve universal health coverage (UHC), including financial risk protection, access to quality essential healthcare services and access to safe,effective, quality and affordable essential medicines and vaccines for all.
Under NRHM, Indian Public Health Standards (IPHS) provides optimal specialized care to the community and achieve and maintain an acceptable standard of quality of care.
It will also foster improved regulation in procurement,strengthened capacity laboratories including their accreditation, establishment of nation-wide quality control systems etc.
