Smokeless tobacco use is also associated with cancers of the lip, oral cavity, pharynx, digestive, respiratory and intrathoracic organs .
It is widely used in home building materials, automotive parts and textiles.
Asbestos fibres are microscopic in nature and when inhaled, get lodged in the soft internal tissue of respiratory system and can irritate the lungs.
Workplace exposure to arsenic, chromium, diesel exhaust, silica and nickel can also increase the risk of developing lung cancer and it is higher for those who also smoke.
The main sources of indoor radon are soil, construction material, and the natural gas used for cooking.
